  "problem": "The value $V(t)$ of Diana's plot of land, in thousands of dollars, can be modeled by the function $V(t)=30\\cdot (1.1)^{t},$ where $t$ is the time in years since she bought the land. What is the growth in the value of the plot over the first three years? Round your answer to the nearest thousand dollars.\n\nDiana's land grew in value by approximately\n{{field-1}}\n thousand dollars over the first three years.",
